<newsitem itemid="201066" id="root" date="1996-11-19" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Unigate H1 profits edge higher.</title>
<headline>Unigate H1 profits edge higher.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		19.0		   vs 18.8</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 7.0		    vs  6.65</p>
<p> Pretax		     60.6		   vs 60.4</p>
<p> Turnover		  1.188 bln	     vs 1.043 bln</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 57 to 59 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 59.3		   vs 55.4</p>
<p> Interest		   1.3 received	 vs 6.4 paid</p>
<p> Tax			  15.8		   vs 16.3</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 3, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  December 3, 1996</p>
<p> Ex-div date		25 November, 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Unigate said overall it continued to perform in line with expectations and at similar levels to last year, but its dairy business was being affected by weak commodity prices.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
